Finding: {"title":"Autosave failure in curriculum-detail.tsx is silent — violates the project's own documented anti-pattern","severity":"HIGH","area":"Data integrity / silent failure","files":["src/components/features/mvp-v2/pages/curriculum-detail.tsx"],"detail":"In the debounced autosave effect (lines 996-1037), when the PUT to `/curriculum/:id/detail` returns `!res.ok` (line 1020-1024), the code does `console.error(...)` and `return` — no `toast.error`, no UI state change, nothing visible to the user. Compare to `handleVersionModalConfirm` (lines 1064-1074) which correctly calls `toast.error` on the same failure condition against the same endpoint.","impact":"A user editing a locked, high-value curriculum (PDD-009 surface) can have their in-progress edits silently fail to persist — e.g. after a transient 5xx, an auth session hiccup, or a payload validation rejection — while the UI shows no error. The user believes the curriculum is saved; a page refresh or another admin's concurrent load will show stale/lost data. This directly matches the exact anti-pattern the project's CLAUDE.md calls out under 'Silent Catch Blocks Prohibited' (though that section is written for empty-list fetches, the underlying principle — user must be told when a save silently fails — applies squarely here).","recommendation":"Add `toast.error('Failed to save changes — please retry')` (and consider a persistent 'unsaved changes' indicator) in the `!res.ok` branch at line 1020-1024, matching the explicit-save handler's behavior.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

